# TIGER behaviour-supervision sample arms and the hyperbolic repair arms.
# These two families were missing an un-ignore block entirely, so the generic
# `logs/` rule above shadowed every one of their Stage 3 native outputs. The
# effect was that Exp1a resample -- the best model in the repository at
# test_R@10 = 0.063633 -- had its SID tracked while its own test_final.json,
# checkpoint and metrics stream were silently dropped, which is exactly what
# CLAUDE.md section 13 forbids. Same shape as the tiger_fork_* block above:
# un-ignore the directory itself first, because git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, then its contents, then the binaries the global
# **/*.pth and **/*.npy rules would otherwise drop.
