# The stage-0 split files are the data every Stage 2 and Stage 3 result in this
# repository is built from, and the offline behaviour analysis reads them
# directly. Without them no committed metric can be recomputed from a clone.
# Re-included after the global **/*.parquet rule above.
!results/stage0_build_parquet/
!results/stage0_build_parquet/*.parquet

# The frozen positive/negative pair index for the behaviour analysis. It is the
# input every published sharing rate, gap and enrichment ratio was computed
# from, so it has to travel with the reports or those numbers cannot be checked.
# Re-included after the global **/*.npz rule, scoped to this one directory.
!results/stage3_T5Train/monotonicity/behavior_pairs.npz

# The canonical seed-42 behaviour pair set the whole programme shares. Every
# arm is measured on exactly these pairs, so the file has to travel with the
# results or the sharing rates cannot be recomputed. Scoped to this one path.
!results/stage3_T5Train/monotonicity/behavior_pairs_s42.npz

# The Louvain behaviour partition the step 4 cluster-consistency term supervises.
# Recorded so the clustering cannot drift between the diagnostic and a run.
# Scoped to this one path, after the global **/*.npz rule.
!results/stage3_T5Train/monotonicity/behaviour_clusters_s42.npz

# The INDEPENDENT validation pair set (step 7): the positives come from
# valid.parquet and every one of them is a held-out interaction, so the scored
# relations never entered training. It travels with the results for the same
# reason as the train-based set: the reported sharing rates and enrichment
# ratios cannot be recomputed without it. Scoped to this one path.
!results/stage3_T5Train/monotonicity/behavior_pairs_valid_s42.npz

# 2026-10-19 (issue #71): the R4/R5 gradient-integrity audit must publish its small run logs and
# manifests as evidence, while the blanket logs/ rule above stays in force everywhere else.
!results/stage2_RQ-VAE/r45_gradient_integrity_audit/logs/
!results/stage2_RQ-VAE/r45_gradient_integrity_audit/logs/**
# 2026-10-19 (issue #71): the DDP audit persists its per-rank tensors only so the parent process can
# read them back; they are multi-MB scratch, the small JSON summaries are the evidence.
results/stage2_RQ-VAE/r45_gradient_integrity_audit/logs/ddp_artifacts/*.pt

# 2026-10-19 (CGV): per-rank gradient tensors exist only so the G5 parent process can read them
# back across the process boundary; the JSON summaries and the certificates are the evidence.
results/stage2_RQ-VAE/_cgv/g5_*/*.pt
